# kuma-off.caddy -- imported at the END of the Caddyfile (top level) when
# KUMA_ENABLED=off (the default). INTENTIONALLY EMPTY: no kuma.DOMAIN site is
# defined, so Caddy neither listens for that hostname nor requests a
# certificate for it (in ACME mode that would need public DNS for
# kuma.DOMAIN). Caddy logs "Import file is empty" for it at start -- a
# warning, not an error. The S6 monitoring profile sets KUMA_ENABLED=on,
# which imports kuma-on.caddy instead.
